      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For some, peace might finally come only when the self-imposed penance ends, making the final line the only honest truth for a man who has paid every debt he ever incurred. There is no other ending that does not feel like a lie when the journey was defined by endless, futile labor against an unavoidable stillness. True relief for his kind often arrives precisely where the character decides to stop asking for forgiveness and instead demands the absolute final cessation of everything.",
      "source": "target",
